# Metrics

Add metrics by mirroring a neighbor in the same file (e.g. `MAEMetric` in `monai/metrics/regression.py`). Load only that neighbor.

## Class

- Subclass the right base: regression metrics subclass `RegressionMetric`; others subclass `CumulativeIterationMetric`.
- Implement only `_compute_metric(self, y_pred, y) -> torch.Tensor` returning a per-batch-item tensor shaped `(batch, 1)`; the base `aggregate()` handles batch reduction.
- Optional `__init__` calls `super().__init__(reduction=..., get_not_nans=...)`.
- Metric lifecycle: instantiate → `metric(y_pred, y)` → `metric.aggregate()`.

## Register

- Add the class name to the correct `from .<module> import (...)` block in `monai/metrics/__init__.py`, case-insensitive alphabetical. No per-file `__all__`.

## Always

- Apache header; `from __future__ import annotations`; Google docstrings; American English.
- Use `torch.quantile(x, 0.5)` (not `torch.median`) when you need the numpy-compatible median.

Full skeleton + named neighbor: `docs/cursor-kit/monai-refs/metrics.md`.

